---
import CommercialLayout from '../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
import BriefForm from '../components/services/BriefForm.astro';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Custom business tools"
  description="Separately scoped internal tools, dashboards, reviewed document processing, quote preparation, and staff knowledge assistants."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="commercial-shell page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="commercial-title">
          A small internal tool still needs a hard boundary.
        </h1><p>
          Custom work is appropriate when an existing tool or one workflow
          cannot solve the operating problem. Every proposal names one problem,
          one approver, a data boundary, and an acceptance test.
        </p><div class="commercial-actions">
          <a
            class="commercial-action"
            href="/brief/?source=custom-tools&service=custom"
            >Describe the internal problem</a
          ><a
            class="commercial-action commercial-action--text"
            href="/workflows/">Could one workflow solve it?</a>
        </div>
      </div><p class="page-intro__note">
        Secondary offer<br /><strong>Separately scoped and supported</strong><br
        />Uses the same single active-project capacity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Selective tools for work that already has an owner.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          Good candidates reduce a bounded manual burden while keeping review
          and decision authority with staff.
        </p>
      </div><div class="boundary-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Internal dashboards</h3><p>
            One operational view with named source systems, viewers, freshness
            expectations, and decision boundaries.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Reviewed document processing</h3><p>
            Extraction, classification, or drafting where a named person
            approves the output before it is used.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Quote preparation</h3><p>
            Rules and source data produce a reviewable draft; pricing approval
            and customer communication stay with staff.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Staff knowledge assistants</h3><p>
            Answers grounded in approved internal sources, with citations,
            permissions, and a clear “cannot answer” state.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Published floors prevent a false small-project promise.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          A genuinely bounded custom build has a broad $5,500 floor. Web App
          Discovery remains $3,500–$5,000 and internal tools commonly begin at
          $15,000+. AI discovery or Blueprint remains $3,500–$10,000; production
          automation commonly begins at $10,000–$30,000. A smaller scope is
          quoted only after it is actually evaluated.
        </p>
      </div><p>
        No speculative product build, business-running agent, or regulated
        autonomous decision system is offered here. Workflow Setup ($3,000) and
        Care ($500/month) do not include a custom tool.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Discovery is useful when the acceptance test is not ready.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          Custom discovery retains its existing rule: 50% of the discovery fee
          credits to the kickoff Project Retainer if the project proceeds within
          30 days, capped at that Project Retainer, with no rollover. That rule
          does not apply to the separate $1,200 Integration Triage.
        </p>
      </div><a href="/discovery/">Review the existing discovery products</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="commercial-shell">
    <BriefForm
      service="custom"
      source="custom-tools"
      context="Custom business tool inquiry"
      heading="Describe the operating problem"
    />
  </div>
</CommercialLayout>
